<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><Content><Views><ViewDef id="c0570001-1111-4a00-b000-000000000001"><Title>Rightsizing - Oversized Candidates</Title><Description>ESXi virtual machines ranked by monthly reclaimable cost. The memory and vCPU rightsizing opportunity from VCF Operations own demand analysis (vCPU Oversized = allocated minus recommended vCPU). Memory Oversized percent = (allocated - recommended) / allocated. Peak Workload % (95th) is peak active / allocated over the window - a raw usage cross-check on the demand recommendation: low (green) confirms the shrink is safe, high (red) means the VM genuinely uses its RAM so trust it over the recommendation. Active and Consumed sit side by side as the actionability context: a large gap (Consumed high, Active low) often means the guest holds cache or heap - confirm the guest memory model (database buffer pool, JVM heap, k8s requests) before shrinking. Sorted by reclaimable cost (USD per month), then by Memory Reclaimable (GB) - so a VM that is clearly oversized but that the cost engine attributed no dollar to (a blank cost) still surfaces on its gigabyte opportunity rather than sinking to the bottom.</Description><SubjectType adapterKind="VMWARE" resourceKind="VirtualMachine" type="descendant"/><SubjectType adapterKind="VMWARE" resourceKind="VirtualMachine" type="self"/><Usage>dashboard</Usage><Usage>report</Usage><Usage>details</Usage><Usage>content</Usage><Controls><Control id="tis_1" type="time-interval-selector" visible="false"><Property name="advancedTimeMode" value="false"/><Property name="unit" value="DAYS"/><Property name="count" value="7"/></Control><Control id="as_2" type="attributes-selector" visible="false"><Property name="attributeInfos"><List><Item><Value><Property name="objectType" value="RESOURCE"/><Property name="attributeKey" value="cost|reclaimableCost"/><Property name="preferredUnitId" value="currency"/><Property name="isStringAttribute" value="false"/><Property name="adap